From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:49:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] native: accept libinput 1.27

Fedora 41 ships libinput 1.27.1 and Alpine 3.21 ships 1.27.0. With the
eraser button (1.29) and plugin system (1.30) calls behind the checks
of the earlier patch, the code needs no libinput API newer than 1.26: a
build on Fedora 41 imports symbols up to the LIBINPUT_1.26 node only.

Nothing is lost compared with libinput 1.28.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 4fcd43c13..6c668d9da 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ wayland_server_req = '>= 1.23'
 wayland_protocols_req = '>= 1.44'
 
 # native backend version requirements
-libinput_req = '>= 1.28.0'
+libinput_req = '>= 1.27.0'
 gbm_req = '>= 21.3'
 libdrm_req = '>= 2.4.118'
 
